# README - Stack Operations

## Aim
This folder demonstrates basic stack operations using an array and a linked list.

---

## Algorithm
1. Initialize the stack as empty.
2. Push each new value onto the top.
3. Pop a value from the top, reporting when the stack is empty.
4. Check whether the stack is empty and, in the linked-list implementation, display its values.

---

## How it works
A stack follows the LIFO (Last In, First Out) principle. The last inserted element is removed first. The array implementation has a capacity of 100; in the linked-list implementation, the head acts as the top of the stack.

---

## Functionality
- Push an element onto the stack
- Pop the top element
- Check whether the stack is empty
- Display the contents in the linked-list implementation

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Push / Pop: O(1)
- Display: O(n) in the linked-list implementation
- Extra space: O(1) fixed array storage (capacity 100) or O(n) linked-list storage
